Microsoft Store Not Opening

Issue (What the user sees/experiences):
- Clicking Microsoft Store does nothing or it crashes immediately.
-  Error messages like “This app can’t open” or “Store isn’t available” may appear.
- Store tiles might be blank, or the app opens briefly then closes.

Cause (Root cause or most likely cause):
- Corrupted Store app or registration.
- Missing or damaged system files.
- Outdated Windows updates.
- Conflicting user profile or temporary data.

Steps / Resolution (Numbered steps, commands, settings):

1. Restart the computer
- Clears temporary glitches or stuck processes.
2. Run Windows Update
- Install any pending updates, restart if needed.
3.Repair or Reset the Store app
Settings: Apps - Apps & Features - Microsoft Store - Advanced Options - Repair / Reset


[ScreenShot1.png]


4. Re-register Microsoft Store via PowerShell
> make surea APPS Closed
   	Open PowerShell 
   Run:
     Get-AppXPackage -AllUsers | Foreach {Add-AppxPackage -DisableDevelopmentMode -Register "$($_.InstallLocation)\AppXManifest.xml"}
   - rebuilds app registration for all built-in apps.


[ScrennShot2.png]


5. Check for corrupted user profile
Log in with another user account
 If Store works there, back up user data and create a new profile.

6. Run SFC / DISM
   - sfc /scannow - repairs system files.
- DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHeal -> fixes files SFC cant

7. Check network connectivity
- Microsoft Store requires internet access; ensure a firewall and or proxy is blocking it.

Why It Happened & Why the Fix Worked 
- Store app registration or its dependencies were corrupted, preventing the app from launching.
- Re-registering the app restores its manifest and connections to system files
- Resetting or creating a new user profile removes profile-specific corruption..
- Repairing system files with SFC/DISM ensures all required Windows components are intact.
